# Known divergence: a gateway-answered portal keeps no position.
#
# `SELECT 1 AS one` is a constant-only SELECT that the multigateway evaluates
# itself, without a backend. PostgreSQL's portal remembers how far it has been
# read: a second Execute of a completed portal returns no rows and
# CommandComplete(SELECT 0), and an Execute whose maxrows equals the rows
# available returns PortalSuspended instead of CommandComplete. The
# multigateway's evaluated portal has no such state, so every Execute returns
# the row and CommandComplete(SELECT 1) again, and maxrows is ignored. No
# supported driver re-executes a completed portal (each execution binds a fresh
# portal), and a driver fetching with a row limit simply finishes one round
# early, so the divergence is recorded rather than fixed. Removing it would
# need a per-portal done flag and PortalSuspended support in the gateway.
#
# Effect: replace PostgreSQL's empty re-execution and suspension with the
# repeated DataRow/CommandComplete(SELECT 1) the multigateway produces.
--- a
+++ b
@@ -10,10 +10,12 @@
 <= BE BindComplete
 <= BE DataRow
 <= BE CommandComplete(SELECT 1)
-<= BE CommandComplete(SELECT 0)
+<= BE DataRow
+<= BE CommandComplete(SELECT 1)
 <= BE BindComplete
 <= BE DataRow
-<= BE PortalSuspended
-<= BE CommandComplete(SELECT 0)
+<= BE CommandComplete(SELECT 1)
+<= BE DataRow
+<= BE CommandComplete(SELECT 1)
 <= BE ReadyForQuery(I)
 FE=> Terminate
